Jozu is a native Swift/SwiftUI language-learning companion (Mac first, iPhone later).

Before doing work, read:

1. `.jozu/HANDOFF.md`
2. `.jozu/STATUS.md`
3. `.jozu/DECISIONS.md` if the task touches architecture

This is the only project-management source of truth. Do not invent a second tracker.

After completing work, update `HANDOFF.md` and `STATUS.md`. Move backlog items in `.jozu/BACKLOG.md` when their state changes. Record new locked choices in `.jozu/DECISIONS.md`.

Native Swift only. No React/Electron/JS unless a later decision explicitly overrides that.

This cloud environment is Linux. The Mac app cannot be compiled or launched here. Do not pretend a local GUI run happened.
